1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:10,950
Dan, please buy four carrots, three tomatoes, and one cucumber. The blue list is for my salad.

2
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:26,550
And six potatoes, two onions, and some broccoli for my soup. Two lists, Dan. Please keep them separate.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Shopping list. List.

4
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,000
A list names things to buy.

5
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Say: a shopping list.

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,000
A shopping list.

7
00:00:50,750 --> 00:00:53,750
Blue soup, yellow salad. Easy!

8
00:00:54,050 --> 00:01:01,850
Dad, that is already backward. Maybe your pocket needs a better filing system.

9
00:01:05,750 --> 00:01:10,550
We can help. I will check the vegetables.

10
00:01:10,850 --> 00:01:18,050
And I will carry the basket. Does broccoli need a seat belt?

11
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Blue bag. Yellow bag.

12
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,000
This bag is blue. Use is.

13
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Say it with me.

14
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:40,000
This bag is blue.

15
00:01:40,750 --> 00:01:50,950
Welcome to the market, team. We need vegetables, not surprises. Stay together, and let's check every item.

16
00:01:55,750 --> 00:02:01,750
Can you carry the basket, Dad? It is very heavy.

17
00:02:02,050 --> 00:02:04,450
But it is empty!

18
00:02:04,750 --> 00:02:07,750
I am practicing for later.

19
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Basket. Carry the basket.

20
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Can you makes a request.

21
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Ask: Can you carry it?

22
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Can you carry it?

23
00:02:30,750 --> 00:02:32,550
Forty carrots, please.

24
00:02:32,850 --> 00:02:35,250
Four, Dad. Four carrots.

25
00:02:35,550 --> 00:02:40,950
Good catch. Forty would need their own shopping cart.

26
00:02:45,750 --> 00:02:49,350
One, two, three, four. Four carrots.

27
00:02:49,650 --> 00:02:55,650
Exactly. I was just checking whether you were paying attention.

28
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Carrot. Four carrots.

29
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Add S for more than one.

30
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Say: I need four carrots.

31
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:20,000
I need four carrots.

32
00:03:20,750 --> 00:03:26,150
We need three tomatoes. These are red and ripe.

33
00:03:26,450 --> 00:03:28,850
Three little bowling balls?

34
00:03:29,150 --> 00:03:33,350
Only if you want tomato soup everywhere.

35
00:03:35,750 --> 00:03:42,350
One tomato, three tomatoes. I have the words and the numbers.

36
00:03:42,650 --> 00:03:46,850
Great. Now keep the tomatoes round, please.

37
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Tomato. Tomatoes.

38
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:58,000
This plural ends in E S.

39
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Say: three tomatoes.

40
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:10,000
Three tomatoes.

41
00:04:10,750 --> 00:04:15,550
A cucumber! Long, green, and ready for salad.

42
00:04:15,850 --> 00:04:23,050
That is a zucchini, Dad. The cucumber is in the next crate.

43
00:04:25,750 --> 00:04:30,550
This is a cucumber. That is a zucchini.

44
00:04:30,850 --> 00:04:36,850
Two green cousins. I should have checked their names first.

45
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Cucumber. Listen: cucumber.

46
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:48,000
This is a cucumber.

47
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Now say the sentence.

48
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:00,000
This is a cucumber.

49
00:05:00,750 --> 00:05:06,150
Six potatoes for the salad. That sounds very crunchy.

50
00:05:06,450 --> 00:05:12,450
Maybe we should check which list belongs to which dish.

51
00:05:15,750 --> 00:05:19,950
How many potatoes do we need? Six.

52
00:05:20,250 --> 00:05:28,650
Six potatoes. I can count them. I just cannot decide where they are going.

53
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Potato. Six potatoes.

54
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:38,000
Use how many for counted things.

55
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
Ask: How many potatoes?

56
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:50,000
How many potatoes?

57
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:54,950
These onions are making me cry already.

58
00:05:55,250 --> 00:06:02,450
You have not cut them, Dad. Maybe they heard your potato-salad plan.

59
00:06:05,750 --> 00:06:11,150
One onion, two onions. Which bag do they need?

60
00:06:11,450 --> 00:06:18,050
An excellent question. Let us keep the evidence together for now.

61
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Onion. Two onions.

62
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:28,000
Use two with a plural noun.

63
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:31,000
Now say the sentence.

64
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:40,000
We need two onions.

65
00:06:40,750 --> 00:06:47,950
Look! A tiny tree. Can we plant a forest in the basket?

66
00:06:48,250 --> 00:06:53,050
It is broccoli, Max. A very tasty-looking forest.

67
00:06:55,750 --> 00:06:59,950
We need some broccoli for Nina's soup.

68
00:07:00,250 --> 00:07:03,850
Then the forest is going swimming.

69
00:07:04,150 --> 00:07:07,750
Finally, one vegetable knows its destination.

70
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:14,000
Broccoli. Some broccoli.

71
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:18,000
We say some broccoli here.

72
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:21,000
Your turn: some broccoli.

73
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:30,000
Some broccoli.

74
00:07:30,750 --> 00:07:35,550
A bell pepper. I cannot hear the bell.

75
00:07:35,850 --> 00:07:42,450
It is named for its shape, Dad. It does not ring.

76
00:07:45,750 --> 00:07:51,750
Maya wants one red bell pepper, not a green one.

77
00:07:52,050 --> 00:07:58,050
Red pepper, silent bell. I am learning so much today.

78
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Bell pepper. Red bell pepper.

79
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:08,000
Put the color before the noun.

80
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:11,000
Say: a red bell pepper.

81
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:20,000
A red bell pepper.

82
00:08:20,750 --> 00:08:24,350
We need two ears of corn.

83
00:08:24,650 --> 00:08:28,250
Ears? Can the corn hear us?

84
00:08:28,550 --> 00:08:33,350
Only if you tell a very corny joke.

85
00:08:35,750 --> 00:08:39,950
Two ears of corn for the soup.

86
00:08:40,250 --> 00:08:45,650
Please do not tell the onions about the forest.

87
00:08:45,950 --> 00:08:48,950
Our shopping has secrets now.

88
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:54,000
Corn. An ear of corn.

89
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:58,000
Two ears of corn.

90
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:01,000
Now say the phrase.

91
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:10,000
Two ears of corn.

92
00:09:10,750 --> 00:09:15,550
This lettuce looks like a green bowling ball.

93
00:09:15,850 --> 00:09:22,450
That one is cabbage. We need the loose-leaf lettuce beside it.

94
00:09:25,750 --> 00:09:29,350
This lettuce has loose, curly leaves.

95
00:09:29,650 --> 00:09:33,850
So do I on a windy morning.

96
00:09:34,150 --> 00:09:38,350
Your hair is not on either list.

97
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Lettuce. Cabbage. Different vegetables.

98
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:48,000
This is lettuce.

99
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Now name the lettuce.

100
00:09:56,000 --> 00:10:00,000
This is lettuce.

101
00:10:00,750 --> 00:10:06,150
One bag of spinach. That is the last item.

102
00:10:06,450 --> 00:10:13,050
Wonderful. My basket is full, and my memory is almost full.

103
00:10:15,750 --> 00:10:19,950
Wait. Blue says salad. Yellow says soup.

104
00:10:20,250 --> 00:10:26,850
Your vegetables are correct. Your two dinner plans have changed places.

105
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Spinach. A bag of spinach.

106
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:38,000
We count the bag here.

107
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Now say the phrase.

108
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:50,000
A bag of spinach.

109
00:10:50,750 --> 00:10:54,350
How is my salad coming along?

110
00:10:54,650 --> 00:10:57,050
Six potatoes and broccoli.

111
00:10:57,350 --> 00:11:03,350
That sounds like Nina's soup wearing a salad name tag.

112
00:11:05,750 --> 00:11:08,750
Could you repeat that, please?

113
00:11:09,050 --> 00:11:16,250
We need salad and soup, not an argument between potatoes and tomatoes.

114
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:24,000
Repeat means say it again.

115
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Could you repeat that, please?

116
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:31,000
Now ask politely.

117
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:40,000
Could you repeat that?

118
00:11:40,750 --> 00:11:47,350
I mixed up the lists. I wanted to get everything right.

119
00:11:47,650 --> 00:11:54,250
You can make a mistake and still be a good dad.

120
00:11:55,750 --> 00:12:02,950
We are a team. Let us read one list at a time.

121
00:12:03,250 --> 00:12:08,650
And no vegetable has to argue with another vegetable.

122
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:14,000
Mixed up means confused.

123
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Mixed describes a past action.

124
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:21,000
Now say the sentence.

125
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:30,000
I mixed up the lists.

126
00:12:30,750 --> 00:12:37,350
Maya's salad: carrots, tomatoes, cucumber, lettuce, and a red bell pepper.

127
00:12:37,650 --> 00:12:41,250
Blue list, blue bag. Everything matches.

128
00:12:45,750 --> 00:12:50,550
Nina's soup: potatoes, onions, broccoli, corn, and spinach.

129
00:12:50,850 --> 00:12:56,850
Yellow list, yellow bag. The forest found its swimming pool!

130
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:04,000
Maya's bag. Nina's bag.

131
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:08,000
Apostrophe S shows belonging.

132
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:11,000
Now name Maya's bag.

133
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:20,000
This is Maya's bag.

134
00:13:20,750 --> 00:13:23,150
How much is everything?

135
00:13:23,450 --> 00:13:26,450
Eighteen dollars and fifty cents.

136
00:13:26,750 --> 00:13:31,550
Good. The teamwork was free, but extremely valuable.

137
00:13:35,750 --> 00:13:39,950
We have twenty dollars. That is enough.

138
00:13:40,250 --> 00:13:47,450
Here you go. One twenty. I checked the number twice this time.

139
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:54,000
Price. Eighteen dollars, fifty cents.

140
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:58,000
How much is it?

141
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:01,000
Now ask the price.

142
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:10,000
How much is it?

143
00:14:10,750 --> 00:14:15,550
Your change is one dollar and fifty cents.

144
00:14:15,850 --> 00:14:19,450
Change? Do we need new clothes?

145
00:14:19,750 --> 00:14:23,350
This change is money coming back.

146
00:14:25,750 --> 00:14:29,950
Twenty minus eighteen fifty is one fifty.

147
00:14:30,250 --> 00:14:38,050
The receipt is right, the bags are right, and I am finally right.

148
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:44,000
Change. Receipt. The P is silent.

149
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Here is your change.

150
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:51,000
Now say the sentence.

151
00:14:56,000 --> 00:15:00,000
Here is your change.

152
00:15:00,750 --> 00:15:06,750
Maya, here are your salad vegetables. Blue list, blue bag.

153
00:15:07,050 --> 00:15:13,050
Perfect. And you remembered to bring our children home, too?

154
00:15:15,750 --> 00:15:18,750
All three children. We counted.

155
00:15:19,050 --> 00:15:25,050
And my soup vegetables! Did the broccoli enjoy its trip?

156
00:15:25,350 --> 00:15:28,950
It asked for a window seat.

157
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:34,000
Vegetables. Listen: vegetables.

158
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:38,000
Here are the vegetables. Use are.

159
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:41,000
Now say the sentence.

160
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:50,000
Here are the vegetables.

161
00:15:50,750 --> 00:15:56,750
First, wash your hands. Then we will wash the vegetables.

162
00:15:57,050 --> 00:15:58,850
Even the cucumber?

163
00:15:59,150 --> 00:16:01,550
Especially our well-traveled cucumber.

164
00:16:05,750 --> 00:16:11,150
Wash the cucumber. Put it on the clean plate.

165
00:16:11,450 --> 00:16:15,050
Exactly. You are giving clear instructions.

166
00:16:15,350 --> 00:16:18,350
My cucumber understands English now.

167
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:24,000
Wash. Wash the cucumber.

168
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:28,000
Instructions can start with a verb.

169
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:31,000
Now give the instruction.

170
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Wash the cucumber.

171
00:16:40,750 --> 00:16:43,150
Shopping finished. Dinner finished!

172
00:16:43,450 --> 00:16:50,650
You brought the ingredients, Dan. They have not learned to cook themselves.

173
00:16:50,950 --> 00:16:53,950
That is tomorrow's English lesson.

174
00:16:55,750 --> 00:17:01,750
First, we prepare the vegetables. Then we make the salad.

175
00:17:02,050 --> 00:17:08,050
And I cook the soup. Two dishes, one happy kitchen.

176
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:14,000
First. Then.

177
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:18,000
These words show the order.

178
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:21,000
Say: First, wash. Then, cook.

179
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:30,000
First, wash. Then, cook.

180
00:17:30,750 --> 00:17:36,150
I felt embarrassed because I mixed up the lists.

181
00:17:36,450 --> 00:17:43,650
We helped because we love you. You help us learn every day.

182
00:17:45,750 --> 00:17:49,950
You listened, asked questions, and tried again.

183
00:17:50,250 --> 00:17:56,850
That is a good recipe for learning. Even without forty carrots.

184
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Because gives a reason.

185
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:08,000
We helped because we care.

186
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:11,000
Your turn: because we care.

187
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:20,000
Because we care.

188
00:18:20,750 --> 00:18:23,750
If you are unsure, ask.

189
00:18:24,050 --> 00:18:28,850
And if a vegetable has ears, speak politely.

190
00:18:29,150 --> 00:18:32,150
That second rule is optional.

191
00:18:35,750 --> 00:18:43,550
I will ask when I am unsure. Could you check this with me?

192
00:18:43,850 --> 00:18:49,250
Of course. Asking for help is always welcome here.

193
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:54,000
Unsure means not certain.

194
00:18:54,000 --> 00:18:58,000
If you are unsure, ask.

195
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:01,000
Now give the advice.

196
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:10,000
If you are unsure, ask.

197
00:19:10,750 --> 00:19:14,950
Tomorrow, we need fruit for a picnic.

198
00:19:15,250 --> 00:19:17,050
One list, please.

199
00:19:17,350 --> 00:19:19,750
One list. Two colors.

200
00:19:20,050 --> 00:19:22,450
And three excellent helpers.

201
00:19:25,750 --> 00:19:38,350
Today we brought home vegetables, new words, and a better plan. One family, one team. See you at the fruit shop!

202
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:44,000
Look at these three vegetables.

203
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:48,000
You know their names now.

204
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:51,000
Say all three names.

205
00:19:56,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Carrot, tomato, cucumber.
